# install --boot (typed): BOOT, a FAT32 volume tools/mkfs made, made a
# Raspberry Pi 5's boot partition from stand-ins for the Pi's /boot, in
# /etc/boot here, since QEMU's initramfs has none: its files copied, a
# device tree among them, and input.bin, an initramfs of the system
# running, written beside them, with no note that the card needs the
# Pi's device trees (install_test has the note itself; a second run
# without one would take this boot past e2e's two minutes). --root data
# makes its cmdline.txt boot data, an L0FS volume of a fixed UUID. Then
# refused with no boot files, onto no volume, and with the boot volume
# as its own root.
start /bin/sh
start /sbin/uart noecho
start /sbin/virtio-blk
start /sbin/fs
dev /sbin/uart
dev /sbin/virtio-blk
